  "distractor_rules": {
    "roots": [
      "The stem is a short kid-world frame about home, family, school, or a trip. It is not one of the four answer sentences.",
      "Exactly one choice is correctly punctuated. Never write two choices that can both look right.",
      "For city and state or city and country, always include the version with no comma.",
      "Other wrong choices move the comma, swap a period for the comma, reverse the city and state, or split a two-word place.",
      "Every choice is a full sentence. Use only the roots word list plus allowed extra place names. Never use real person names; use <NAME>.",
      "Never use street numbers, brands, or grown-up addresses. Keep places in the kid world: home, school, trips, family.",
      "Tier 3 wrong choices must be near-miss comma placement, not silly extra marks."
    ]
  },
